#!/usr/bin/env briar
# Radix

The importing program. `folium` is reached three ways (directly, via
`media`, via `sub/ramus`): members in post-order are folium, media,
ramus - each once.

<bibliotheca via="media.thistle"/>
<bibliotheca via="folium.thistle"/>
<bibliotheca via="sub/ramus.thistle"/>

<c!>
s32
principale (vacuum)
{
    FoliumRes r;

    r.valor = media_quadruplicare(V) + ramus_octuplicare(I);
    imprimere("%d\n", (integer)r.valor);
    redde ZEPHYRUM;
}
</c>

The test region sees the members too (the lapide case: recensio's tests
call textus's projection).

<c! munus="probatio">
s32
principale (vacuum)
{
    Piscina*  piscina = piscina_generare_dynamicum("probatio", 4096);
    FoliumRes r;

    credo_aperire(piscina);
    r = media_res(III);
    CREDO_AEQUALIS_S32(r.valor, XII);
    CREDO_AEQUALIS_S32(folium_duplicare(VII), XIV);
    CREDO_AEQUALIS_S32(ramus_octuplicare(II), XVI);
    credo_imprimere_compendium();
    redde credo_omnia_praeterierunt() ? ZEPHYRUM : I;
}
</c>
